# resampledmo: Implement IMediaObject::GetInputStatus().
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/12389 state=closed
# NAudio 2.0's `WasapiOut` checks the source format with `IAudioClient::IsFormatSupported()` in shared mode and, when the answer is not `S_OK`, inserts the Resampler DMO (`ResamplerDmoStream`). Its `Read()` calls `GetInputStatus()` through `Marshal.ThrowExceptionForHR()` before every `ProcessInput()`, so with the stub the playback thread stops with a `NotImplementedException` and nothing is played.

The resampler is inserted for a source that differs from the mix format in rate or channel count. Wine 11.20, like Windows 10, answers a 48 kHz mono float source with `S_FALSE` and the 48 kHz stereo float mix format as the closest match; Wine 11.0 returned `S_OK` there. Reported as silent received audio in the voice client of vatSys on a Wine 11.20 based build.

The expected values in the test were measured on Windows 10 22H2 (10.0.19045) with the same calls in a standalone program: no flags before both types are set and while an input buffer is held, `DMO_INPUT_STATUSF_ACCEPT_DATA` otherwise, `DMO_E_INVALIDSTREAMINDEX` for stream 1. A `NULL` status pointer crashes there, so it is not tested.
--- dlls/mf/tests/transform.c
+++ dlls/mf/tests/transform.c
